# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=escort spec=paladin:protection
# style=melee view=844x390,touch save=carried.
#
# melee has been run on battlegrounds twice before (hunter:marksmanship on
# Ebb and Flow, shaman:elemental on this same map) and both times read
# hitsPerMin=0 the whole match -- but both were ranged specs forced into
# melee range by melee's own beeline-to-target steering. direction.md's #7
# section names the open question directly: "Worth a melee-style warrior or
# rogue on either map before trusting 'melee style loses' as evidence about
# battlegrounds rather than about pairing a ranged kit with a beeline-to-
# target steering algorithm." paladin:protection is the first melee-capable
# kit this line has given the melee style on any battleground -- and it is
# also a tank, which #7's newest entry (druid:guardian/mash, 2026-09-27)
# found costs a match more than losing an interchangeable dps does, since a
# battleground's five roles are an exact trade (one tank/one healer/three
# damage). So this cell tests two open questions in one pull: does a kit
# that can actually connect at melee range change the hitsPerMin=0 shape,
# and does a passive/ineffective tank cost this match the way the
# guardian's did. carried save is known-fresh-in-disguise per #273 (still
# open), so nothing here relies on anything actually carrying.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
targets
shot bg-menu

tap map:escort
targets
shot escort-picked

tap class:paladin:protection
shot class-picked

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play melee 90
shot mid1
state
bill

wait 5
play melee 90
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play melee 90
shot mid3
state
bill
